
# Project 06 - Database Backup and Disaster Recovery

Campus Facility Maintenance System

## Project Overview

This project explores database backup and disaster recovery using Docker Compose, Apache HTTPD and PostgreSQL within a simulated campus facility maintenance environment.

The project focuses on persistent database storage, physical volume backups, database restoration, recovery verification, network segmentation, resource management and container security hardening.

The primary objective is to develop reliable database recovery procedures while maintaining data integrity, service availability and operational resilience.

## Technical Objectives

- Deploy Apache HTTPD and PostgreSQL containers.
- Configure CPU and memory restrictions.
- Implement frontend and backend network segmentation.
- Restrict direct database exposure.
- Apply least-privilege security controls.
- Maintain persistent database storage.
- Create physical database volume backups.
- Restore database files into a separate Docker volume.
- Verify database records after restoration.
- Retain original database storage until recovery is confirmed.

