Network segmentation reduces unnecessary service exposure while maintaining internal container connectivity.

## Docker Compose Configuration

```yaml
services:
  maintenance:
    image: httpd:2.4
    container_name: facility-web
    ports:
      - "8150:80"
    cpus: 0.9
    mem_limit: 512m
    restart: unless-stopped
    networks:
      - facility-front
      - facility-back
    privileged: false
    cap_drop:
      - ALL
    security_opt:
      - no-new-privileges:true

  database:
    image: postgres:16
    container_name: facility-db
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: facilitydb
      POSTGRES_USER: facilityuser
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?Set password}
    cpus: 0.6
    mem_limit: 640m
    restart: always
    networks:
      - facility-back
    volumes:
      - facility-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data

networks:
  facility-front:
    name: facility-front
    driver: bridge

  facility-back:
    name: facility-back
    driver: bridge

volumes:
  facility-data:
    name: facility-data
```

